aiGrader.prompt:
Q1 — What is the difference between === and ==? Give a short example where they give different results.

Q2 — In the condition `age >= 13 && age <= 19 || hasException`, which operator runs first, && or ||? Explain why adding parentheses around the && part makes the condition easier to read even though it doesn't change the result.

Q3 — Predict what each of these three snippets logs, and explain why in one sentence each.

Snippet A:
let temp = 45;
if (temp < 32) {
  console.log("Freezing");
} else if (temp < 60) {
  console.log("Cold");
} else if (temp < 80) {
  console.log("Warm");
} else {
  console.log("Hot");
}

Snippet B:
let score = 72;
let grade = (score >= 90) ? "A" :
  (score >= 80) ? "B" :
  (score >= 70) ? "C" :
  "D";
console.log(grade);

Snippet C:
let day = "Friday";
console.log(day === "Saturday" || "Sunday");
